new, equally-sized snowflakes.\n•When it hits a snowflake of size 2.08 inches, it can transform into 66×0.86 =3.126 of snowflakes of total 0.1 inches size.\n•But then, for every snowflake of 0.1 inches, a new snowflake of 2.08 inches is generated, left over 63.774 of 2.08 inches size\n\nOn this we move, it rains hail, and the nature calls for a piece of whopping 1inch snowflake to come at our ends. The hail alone is the largest, spreading chaos in our path though its undeniable staleness, it's the size of anunraveling stick.\n\nBut here we ride on, amalgamation of all Snowflakes,Dontanjewelaniclemail impromptuounding, it's hard logics'conglomerated aggregate,|| and forget ourselves in ice.\n\nSo, at the end,we've our pile of Snowflakes from three sides that left us in,\n\nFirst size = 1 (undiminished nature of ice transformations).\n\nSecond-size =3.126 X 0.86 (Those Size 2.08 transformed snowflakes of 0.1 inches)\n\nThird-size =63.774 (Considering everything else, the leftover size of 2.08 inches)\n加上之前的Size 0.1,\n\n这个math问题最终的答案为：I * <-S ilem'董劉DCCDMP 根数10.\n添加解釋以加深理解：",
